**Querying owners by city — no dedicated method exists.** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` defines only: `findByLastName(String)`, `findByLastName(String, Pageable)`, `findById(int)`, `save(Owner)`, `findAll()`, `findAll(Pageable)`, `delete(Owner)`. To query by city today you must call `findAll()` and filter on `getCity()` in code (this is how the existing customer-code sequence is derived — `findAll().size()`). Adding a city prefix keyed on the owner's own `city` needs no repository change (it reads `owner.getCity()`); a per-city sequence/count would need either `findAll()`+filter or a new Spring Data-style `findByCity` method added to this interface and its JPA/JDBC implementations.

